  {
    "claim": "The 17 author-taking dev.code commands declare nn_sessionid (platform-injected on all web calls) and default an empty author to the session user; set_module_flag no longer exists.",
    "detail": "Browser clients pass author:\"\" — journals record the real session displayname. CLI/MCP callers pass author explicitly (provenance names like \"claude\") AND nn_sessionid:\"\" — every declared param required. The builder does not garbage-collect deleted commands: prune the generated .rs and its mod.rs registration by hand after delete_command on a static lib. Clean generated-src commits come from a de-overlay + newbound rebuild + re-overlay cycle (the de-overlayed binary loses the agent commands until re-regenerated — rebuild again after re-overlaying before any archivist call); the regenerated initializer may drop the cmd-scaffold block when data/cmd is absent — restore it rather than committing that noise.",
    "tags": "bench-collapse",
    "confidence": "high",
    "time": 1786406673052
  },
  {
    "claim": "dev.code.set_timer fails under `newbound exec` (add_timer needs the `system` globals that only init_globals creates) - run it through `newbound mcp` instead.",
    "detail": "The failure is late: the timer component record and the control's timer entry are already written when add_timer panics, and the _patches journal entry is skipped. Re-running the same set_timer over mcp replaces the record and journals normally (replace-only semantics heal the partial write). Observed 2026-08-11 wiring dev.code.init.",
    "tags": "set_timer, exec, mcp, globals",
    "confidence": "high",
    "time": 1786419691108
  },
  {
    "claim": "dev.code.init (boot timer, start 0, once) seeds runtime/metaidentity with the default identity \"Some Dev\" when the record is absent, so fresh clones publish without hand-seeding.",
    "detail": "Same pattern as security.security.init: an init timer on the dev.code control. No-op when an identity exists; edit via the workbench publish pane or dev.code.set_meta_identity. Landed on branch claude/metaidentity-startup-init-euh44x (newbound 6018c09); the scratch-instance recipes no longer seed by hand. Timers only fire under `newbound` (run mode) - exec and mcp modes never start timer_loop.",
